# scripts/leak-check.allowed-emails
#
# Addresses the tree legitimately needs. One glob per line, matched
# against the whole lower-cased address; comments and blank lines are
# ignored. Only non-personal, generic addresses belong here — never an
# operator's personal address.

# IANA reserved example domains (AGENT.md "No local-environment leaks")
*@example.com
*@example.org
*@example.net

# SSH clone and noreply forms the tooling and docs legitimately ship with
git@github.com
git@gitlab.com

# IANA-reserved example domains used by webhook/fixture hosts (hooks, peer, datawatch, h, ...).
*.example
*.example.net
# Subdomain hosts of IANA-reserved example domains (fixture git hosts, e.g. gitea.example.com).
*@*.example.com
*@*.example.net
# RFC 2606 never-assigned domains used in test fixtures.
*.invalid
*.local
# IANA-reserved .test domain used for git test identities.
*.test
# systemd user-bus unit names (user@UID.service) referenced in test evidence.
*.service
# GitHub Actions default committer noreply identifier (bot, not a person).
*@users.noreply.github.com

# Retina asset filenames ending @2x.png (screenshot names, not mailboxes).
*@*.png
noreply@*
no-reply@*
